DAX Formulas Used in Motorola Mobile Sales Analysis – Power BI
The following DAX formulas can be used to calculate KPIs and analyze sales performance in thise project.

1. Total Sales
Total Sales =
SUMX(
    Sales,
    Sales[Units Sold] * Sales[Price Per Unit]
)


2. Total Quantity Sold
Total Quantity =
SUM(Sales[Units Sold])


3. Total Transactions
Total Transactions =
DISTINCTCOUNT(Sales[Transaction ID])


4. Average Sales
Average Sales =
AVERAGE(Sales[Price Per Unit])


5. Average Customer Rating
Average Rating =
AVERAGE(Sales[Customer Ratings])


6. Total Brands
Total Brands =
DISTINCTCOUNT(Sales[Brand])


7. Total Cities
Total Cities =
DISTINCTCOUNT(Sales[City])


8. Total Mobile Models
Total Models =
DISTINCTCOUNT(Sales[Mobile Model])


9. Sales by Brand
Brand Sales =
[Total Sales]


Use Brand as the category in your chart.
10. Sales by Month
Monthly Sales =
[Total Sales]


Use Month on the X-axis and Monthly Sales on the Y-axis.
11. Sales by Payment Method
Payment Sales =
[Total Sales]


Use Payment Method as the category.
12. Sales Percentage
Sales Percentage =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Sales],
    CALCULATE(
        [Total Sales],
        ALL(Sales[Brand])
    ),
    0
)


Format this measure as Percentage.

DAX Functions Used in This Project
DAX Function	Purpose
SUM()	Calculate total quantity
SUMX()	Calculate total sales
AVERAGE()	Calculate average sales and ratings
DISTINCTCOUNT()	Count unique transactions
CALCULATE()	Modify filter context
ALL()	Remove filters
DIVIDE()	Perform safe division
DATE()	Create date values
FORMAT()	Format values

Note: Replace Sales with your actual Power BI table name if it is different.
